READING
  1. Total Freiman relation rank is a capacity/envelope variable, not the
     correction itself. AP rows have maximal rank and maximal correction,
     but k=8 already has a high hidden-only odd-coset row with visible
     rank 0 and Corr_y=0.2157.
  2. Rank alone is too coarse.  The same total-rank band can contain rows
     with different visible/hidden ranks and visibly different correction.
     Hidden shells can cancel or reinforce depending on parity/coset sign;
     KPS rows show that bounded weighted rank can be full even when pair
     rank is small.
  3. The next proof lemma should bound correction by a signed/coset rank
     packet: relation rank supplies capacity, while shell phase supplies
     the correction coefficient.

=== Tournament Analysis ===
Hamiltonian path:
  signed_coset_rank > total_freiman_rank > weighted_relation_rank > visible_fold_rank > hidden_shell_rank > correction_per_rank > covolume_short_vector_data > raw_additive_energy > raw_runner_vertices
